#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:35
#: 3e9a010602c04b9a909b7a19a67defad
msgid "For all protocols above, ArduPilot auto-detects the protocol of the RC receiver system. However, depending on the protocol and autopilot type, the physical connection to the autopilot may differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:37
#: 280023475f10485fbdfbef637a88a17f
msgid "Some protocols, most notably SRXL2, CRSF, and ELRS, require a full UART connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:39
#: 256af121180d4a669139ad2979839795
msgid "In addition other protocols that also provide telemetry, like FPort, would generally require a bi-directional half-duplex connection in order to obtain telemetry. For these protocols the TX output of the UART should be connected to the serial input of the receiver. It is also possible on F7 and H7 boards to connect to the UART RX input with some additional configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:42
#: ec709abe060f4ab3a249373d2097083c
msgid "PPM-Sum/SBus/i-BUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:44
#: 5de59a5fd6b84396b4b3d9c82164fabf
msgid "These receivers are usually connected to the RCin or SBUS input pin on the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:46
#: 98ab1924db4a429d9ad7097086c3d055
msgid "To connect a PPM-Sum receiver or an SBus receiver to a Pixhawk, for example, plug the ground (black), power (red) and signal (usually white - orange in the diagram below) wires to the RC pins on the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:53
#: 38550460518e41e3ac60ba6eff8b6816
msgid "The parameter to enable the SBus output from the PixHawk style autopilots is :ref:`BRD_SBUS_OUT<BRD_SBUS_OUT>`. This is only to pass SBus externally to other devices, like servos. Not to connect a receiver to RCin or SBus In."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:58
#: 077352c5501e447b84ff26c89b375d18
msgid "DSM/DSM2/DSM-X/SRXL/SUM-D"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:60
#: ea78715531bf4226a9205957102e4cfa
msgid "For autopilots that do not provide a separate ``DSM`` input, these can be connected as above. However, for performance reasons on autopilots that use an IOMCU (The Pixhawk/Cube family), the autopilot's ``DSM`` input connection is highly recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:66
#: 2256f44c55974eb8b7c97e8ced673c92
msgid "FPort/FPort2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:68
#: 1c3af0a6f77e46b1abdcff9a7bc7d14e
msgid "FPort is a bi-directional protocol, using SBus RC in one direction, and serial telemetry in the other. The RC portion can be decoded when attached to an autopilot as if it were SBus, but the embedded telemetry would be lost. See the :ref:`FPort setup documentation<common-FPort-receivers>` for details on connection to one of the autopilots Serial Ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:72
#: 631f907ca7ae41df8cbce496e083953b
msgid ":ref:`mLRS <common-mlrs-rc>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:74
#: 459a8486590b4a408cca9329d71c105d
msgid "mLRS can provide RC control and MAVLink telemetry. mLRS receivers have an RC output pin that can be configured for either SBUS or CRSF protocol (CRSF would be only RC data). For SBUS you can connect it to the autopilot's RCin pin. For CRSF or SBUS, it can be connected to any autopilot UART RX pin and that port configured for RC protocol. Using CRSF portocol, allows RSSI/LQ information to be delivered to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:76
#: d174c8fc9d11437391cfa775b4c188f6
msgid "For optional telemetry a separate TX/RX port is provided on the receiver to be connected to an autopilot MAVLink telemetry serial port. You can omit the single wire RC connection and configure the mLRS receiver to output RC channels over MAVLink if you are not using GCS RC overrides (eg, joystick)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:80
#: 5b1ae70a05334f8a8c2606a128fd1443
msgid "SRXL2/CRSF/ELRS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:82
#: 2c719da6216b4bd89e93504cb8161c81
msgid "These bi-directional protocols require the use of a Serial Port. See links below for setup and connections."
msgstr ""

