#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:171
#: 9a7024e50e274e1685dfe802adf217c3
msgid "Note 1: DragonLink provides a 56Kbaud transparent link for telemetry, allowing full MAVLink telemetry to/from the vehicle from the transmitter module. Dragonlink is an add-on module to the transmitter, such as an FRSky Taranis or RadioMaster T16. See :ref:`common-dragonlink-rc`. `MTP (Mavlink to Passthru) converters <https://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?3089648-Mavlink-To-FrSky-Passthrough-Converter>`__ are available to allow direct display of MAVLink Telemetry data on OpenTX transmitters using :ref:`Yaapu Telemetry LUA Script<common-frsky-yaapu>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:173
#: fc618bcff98e43ec86950f55ceccf185
msgid "Note 2: See :ref:`common-frsky-yaapu`. The ability to change parameters over FRSky telemetry from an Open TX compatible transmitter in addition to displaying the telemetry data is possible. Most FRSky compatible transmitters use `OpenTX <https://www.open-tx.org/>`__. Note that R9 systems are not quite Long Range, but much further range than normal FRSky systems, themselves at the very high end of the Short Range category at 1.6-2km range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:175
#: 4c48c09d45f846adb18584bd47377fd0
msgid "Note 3: ArduPilot provides a means to send its telemetry data via CRSF such that it can be displayed on `OpenTX <https://www.open-tx.org/>`__ transmitters using the :ref:`Yaapu Telemetry LUA Script<common-frsky-yaapu>`. The ability to change parameters over CRSF telemetry from an Open TX compatible transmitter in addition to displaying the telemetry data is also possible. See :ref:`common-crsf-telemetry`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:177
#: 83fe6d1a80c347459f6d292c540d553b
msgid "Note 4: ELRS (ExpressLRS) is a flexible open-source system that can output CRSF, SBUS, or MAVLink (with embedded RC) protocols. Telemetry requires the use of CRSF or Mavlink, and the receiver must be wired to a full UART.  See `ExpressLRS site <https://www.expresslrs.org/>__`  and :ref:`TBS CRSF/ ELRS <common-tbs-rc>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:179
#: f4bd5881ba5a490dbeba5d8f3f15d497
msgid "Note 5: The mLRS project is firmware designed specifically to carry both RC and MAVLink. The usable telemetry speed varies by the chosen mode and is managed via RADIO_STATUS flow control. It uses the CRSF (TBS Crossfire) RC protocol on both the receiver and Tx module.  It also integrates full MAVLink telemetry via serial connections on the Tx module and the receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:181
#: 664237af034c42df8490b58ad1615167
msgid "Note 6: Vendor Specific Telem means that they accommodate sensor additions to the vehicle and can display the information on certain Vendor specific TXs but do not send ArduPilot telemetry from the vehicle to ArduPilot compatible GCS or OpenTX display scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:183
#: 93c8d563b2ad46f68b7f05120f98123e
msgid "Note 7: The receiver must support i-BUS telemetry (look for a SENS port on the receiver or check the product specifications)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rc-systems.rst:185
#: e57dfb95b57d40f7b3cff256b67744d5
msgid "Note 8: These systems have integrated HD video transmission from Ethernet or HDMI camera systems in addition to RC control and vehicle telemetry."
msgstr ""

